{
  "info": {
    "name": "Healthmarg API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Healthmarg REST API (/api/v1). Import together with local.postman_environment.json and select the \"Healthmarg — Local\" environment.\n\nKept in sync with docs/api.md: every branch that changes an endpoint updates this file. Never store real secrets here."
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "description": "Dependency status. Public.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "200 {status:\"ok\", database, redis} when healthy; 503 {status:\"degraded\"} when MySQL (or an enabled Redis) is down. redis is \"disabled\" locally when REDIS_ENABLED=false."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200 or 503', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 503]));",
                  "pm.test('reports database and redis state', () => { const b = pm.response.json(); pm.expect(b).to.have.keys('status', 'database', 'redis'); });",
                  "pm.test('has rate-limit headers', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.has('RateLimit')).to.be.true);",
                  "pm.test('hides the framework', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.has('X-Powered-By')).to.be.false);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Unknown route returns safe 404",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/does-not-exist",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "does-not-exist"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('404 with generic message', () => { pm.response.to.have.status(404); pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.message).to.eql('Route not found'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "description": "EMAIL FEATURES ARE OFF FOR NOW (EMAIL_ENABLED=false): Register returns 201 and signs you in (409 EMAIL_TAKEN if the email exists); Verify email, Resend, Forgot password and Reset password return 404 until email is switched on.\n\nSign-up, email verification, sign-in (with 2FA), sessions and password reset.\n\nLocally, emails are saved as HTML files in backend/.local/outbox/ (and the link is printed in the API log). Copy the `token` from a link into the matching environment variable.\n\nThe refresh token lives in an HttpOnly cookie that Postman keeps automatically. Refresh/Logout need `GET csrf` first (it sets csrfToken) and send an Origin header, like a browser.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET csrf",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/csrf",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "csrf"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Issues a CSRF token (body) + signed cookie. Needed before Refresh and Logout."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.environment.set('csrfToken', pm.response.json().csrfToken);",
                  "pm.test('csrf token saved', () => pm.expect(pm.environment.get('csrfToken')).to.be.a('string'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\",\n  \"displayName\": \"Asha\",\n  \"acceptTerms\": true,\n  \"acceptPrivacy\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Email off (current): 201 + accessToken (saved automatically) and the refresh cookie, or 409 EMAIL_TAKEN. Email on: always 202, then open the verifyEmail file in backend/.local/outbox/ and copy the token into verifyToken."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 (signed in, email off) or 202 (email on)', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([201, 202]));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) pm.environment.set('accessToken', pm.response.json().accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
